---
function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number) {
  const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
  const p1 = [x2 - 8 * Math.cos(a - 0.45), y2 - 8 * Math.sin(a - 0.45)];
  const p2 = [x2 - 8 * Math.cos(a + 0.45), y2 - 8 * Math.sin(a + 0.45)];
  return {
    line: `M ${x1} ${y1} L ${x2 - 6 * Math.cos(a)} ${y2 - 6 * Math.sin(a)}`,
    head: `${x2},${y2} ${p1[0].toFixed(1)},${p1[1].toFixed(1)} ${p2[0].toFixed(1)},${p2[1].toFixed(1)}`,
  };
}
---
<figure class="gp">
  <div class="gp-scroll">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 900 250" role="img" aria-label="context.Background is the root. WithCancel derives ctx. Worker 1 and worker 2 both use ctx. One cancel call closes ctx.Done and both workers stop.">
    <rect x="20" y="108" width="150" height="44" rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="95" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="strong">context.Background()</text>
    {(() => { const a = arrow(170, 130, 240, 130); return <g class="arrow"><path d={a.line} /><polygon points={a.head} /></g>; })()}
    <text x="205" y="120" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">WithCancel</text>
    <rect x="240" y="108" width="190" height="44" rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="335" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="strong">ctx</text>
    <text x="335" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="red"><tspan data-lang-en>main calls cancel()</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>main gọi cancel()</tspan></text>
    {(() => { const a = arrow(335, 68, 335, 108); return <g class="arrow bad"><path d={a.line} /><polygon points={a.head} /></g>; })()}
    {[
      { y: 40, n: '1' },
      { y: 180, n: '2' },
    ].map((w) => {
      const a = arrow(430, 130, 530, w.y + 20);
      return (
        <g>
          <g class="arrow"><path d={a.line} /><polygon points={a.head} /></g>
          <rect x="530" y={w.y} width="130" height="40" rx="8" class="box" />
          <text x="595" y={w.y + 25} text-anchor="middle" class="strong">worker {w.n}</text>
          <text x="680" y={w.y + 25} class="muted"><tspan data-lang-en>stops: context canceled</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>dừng: context canceled</tspan></text>
        </g>
      );
    })}
    <text x="335" y="178" text-anchor="middle" class="muted"><tspan data-lang-en>ctx.Done() closes</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>ctx.Done() được đóng</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Both workers hold the same ctx, so one cancel() reaches both. A child made with WithTimeout or WithValue from ctx would be canceled too.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Hai worker cùng giữ một ctx, nên một lần cancel() tới được cả hai. Context con tạo từ ctx bằng WithTimeout hay WithValue cũng bị hủy theo.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gp { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gp-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gp svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gp text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .gp .h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp .strong { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp .muted { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp .red { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .gp .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp .box.bad { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .gp .bar { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp .bar.bad { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .gp .wait { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .gp .rule { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .gp .axis { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gp .dot { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp .dot.bad { fill: var(--red); }
  .gp .arrow path { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gp .arrow polygon { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp .arrow.bad path { stroke: var(--red); }
  .gp .arrow.bad polygon { fill: var(--red); }
  .gp figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
